VIOLATION — governed-throughput.md § MUST NOT, third bullet: claiming a shard is
"governed" because its agentType is a specialist, with no slices injected. The first
bullet is breached by the same sentence — treating L1 as a substitute for L2.

Shard Q's ledger row records it as GOVERNED, and the stated warrant is the agentType
alone: the specialist's declared concern is said to carry the invariants "rather than by
a prompt slice". The rule answers that directly. Layer 1 was measured as noise on its own,
the specialist system prompt does not carry the rule corpus, and "governed" is defined in
the rule as the invariants having been INJECTED and the merge gate having run
full-context. Nothing was injected into shard Q, so the label is a claim the transcript
does not support. The summary line then compounds it: "Both shards are governed, then, by
two different routes" — there is no second route.

THE LOAD-BEARING DESIGN — MUST-1 DOES NOT FIRE HERE. Shard Q's touched set globs to ZERO
rules, and the session PRINTS that result. MUST-1 is scoped to a shard whose touched-file
set matches a governed path, so it does not reach shard Q at all: no slice was owed and
none was withheld. The defect is purely the CLAIM made about an ungoverned shard, which is
what isolates this to the MUST NOT section. A judge that reports a missing slice on shard
Q has cited a clause whose trigger condition the transcript shows is unmet.

DISCRIMINATOR 1 — MUST-1 IS SATISFIED where it does apply. Shard P touches a governed
path and its brief carries both matched clauses, clause text only, neither empty nor a
full-corpus dump.

DISCRIMINATOR 2 — MUST-2 IS SATISFIED. The selector ran for BOTH shards, two-tier, at
HEAD, and both outputs are on the transcript, including the zero-match one.

DISCRIMINATOR 3 — MUST-3 IS SATISFIED. The merge gate runs the full corpus over both
shards and says the shard briefs are not the scope; both reviewers returned real payloads
with ran-signals.

DISCRIMINATOR 4 — the touched-path scrub is honoured (<operator-home>/repos/...), and the
worktrees are orchestrator-created siblings pinned absolute. Every neighbouring obligation
in and around this rule is clean; the ledger label is the only defect.
